  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Schools and families value activities that students actually do. They judge you by participation, finished tasks and honest reflection.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is asking a worker one good question.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and career awareness activities for school students: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools can draft question lists and activity plans. Routine planning shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Listening, judgment and real contact with workers hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft question lists and check them; later, own the programme.
  </p>

